<h2>Shopify email app FAQ</h2>
<section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6">
<div><h3>Are these rankings sponsored?</h3><p>No. Guides prioritize operating fit, consent handling, and total cost. Vendor links point to official sources so readers can verify current plans and limits themselves.</p></div>
<div><h3>Which guide should a brand-new store read first?</h3><p>Start with the store-model guide closest to your catalog, then the welcome-series and cart-recovery lifecycle guides. That covers the first ninety days of a realistic email program without overcommitting to a complex platform.</p></div>
<div><h3>How current is the pricing information?</h3><p>We avoid restating specific plan prices because they change frequently. Each guide links to official pricing pages and explains which cost components to model, including overages, SMS credits, and implementation work.</p></div>
<div><h3>Do these guides replace a deliverability audit?</h3><p>No. They help you choose and configure tools. Deliverability itself depends on consent quality, sending history, and infrastructure, which the deliverability guide covers separately.</p></div>
<div><h3>How should I combine guides into a decision?</h3><p>Read one store-model guide, one lifecycle guide, and the selection-framework material, then model cost and suppression requirements across the two or three finalists. Decide with a bounded pilot rather than by feature comparison alone.</p></div>
<div><h3>What if my store model is not covered?</h3><p>Use the closest catalog and buying-cycle analogy, then verify the assumptions that differ. The lifecycle and operating-discipline guides apply to almost any Shopify store regardless of vertical.</p></div>
